  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given, <math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mi>e</mi></mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math><br />Let,&nbsp;<math><mi>g</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></math><br /><math> <mrow> <mo>&#8658;</mo><msup> <mi>g</mi> <mo>&#8242;</mo> </msup> <mfenced> <mi>x</mi> </mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><msup> <mi>x</mi> <mn>2</mn> </msup> <mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mfenced> <mrow> <msup> <mi>x</mi> <mn>2</mn> </msup> <mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow> </mfenced></mrow> </math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>for&#160;</mtext><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mfenced close=\"]\"><mrow><mo>&#8722;</mo><mo>&#8734;</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>0</mn><mtext>&#8201;for&#8201;</mtext><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><math><mo>&#8756;</mo><mi>g</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is increasing as well as decreasing in different intervals<br /><math><mo>&#8756;</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is many-one<br />Now, Range of <math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is <math><mfenced close=\"]\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msup><mrow><mi>e</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></